From: Yusuf Al Zadid <yusufalzadid@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: apr: optional GPR packet tracing

Every client of the DSP - q6apm, q6prm, and userspace through audio_pkt -
sends and receives through this one router, so a tap here sees all of them
without instrumenting any.

That is worth having because of a specific problem: the in-kernel clients
start graphs on this DSP successfully while GSL, driving the same firmware
over the passthrough, is refused at APM_CMD_GRAPH_START for every graph
tried, with a bare error and nothing in the DSP's own (hash-only) log. Six
explanations have been eliminated by testing; what is left is to compare the
two clients' packets directly.

Off by default, toggled at runtime through
/sys/module/apr/parameters/gpr_trace.

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
index a956c407c..e05b239de 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
@@ -20,6 +20,34 @@ enum {
 	PR_TYPE_GPR,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Log every GPR packet in both directions.
+ *
+ * Both the in-kernel clients and userspace (through audio_pkt) reach the DSP
+ * through this one router, so a tap here sees both without having to
+ * instrument either. That is the point: when one client's command succeeds
+ * and another's identical-looking command fails, the only way to settle what
+ * actually differs is to read the bytes.
+ *
+ * Off by default; toggle at runtime:
+ *   echo 1 > /sys/module/apr/parameters/gpr_trace
+ */
+static bool gpr_trace;
+module_param(gpr_trace, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(gpr_trace, "log every GPR packet to and from the DSP");
+
+/* Enough for a header plus a good deal of payload; graphs are far larger. */
+#define GPR_TRACE_MAX 256
+
+static void gpr_trace_pkt(const char *dir, const void *buf, int len)
+{
+	if (!gpr_trace)
+		return;
+
+	print_hex_dump(KERN_INFO, dir, DUMP_PREFIX_OFFSET, 32, 4, buf,
+		       min(len, GPR_TRACE_MAX), false);
+}
+
 /* Some random values tbh which does not collide with static modules */
 #define GPR_DYNAMIC_PORT_START	0x10000000
 #define GPR_DYNAMIC_PORT_END	0x20000000
@@ -132,6 +160,9 @@ static int pkt_router_send_svc_pkt(struct pkt_router_svc *svc, struct gpr_pkt *p
 
 	hdr = &pkt->hdr;
 
+	if (pr->type == PR_TYPE_GPR)
+		gpr_trace_pkt("gpr tx: ", pkt, hdr->pkt_size);
+
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&svc->lock, flags);
 	ret = rpmsg_trysend(pr->ch, pkt, hdr->pkt_size);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&svc->lock, flags);
@@ -274,6 +305,8 @@ static int gpr_do_rx_callback(struct packet_router *gpr, struct apr_rx_buf *abuf
 	if (ver > GPR_PKT_VER + 1)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	gpr_trace_pkt("gpr rx: ", buf, len);
+
 	hdr_size = hdr->hdr_size;
 	if (hdr_size < GPR_PKT_HEADER_WORD_SIZE) {
 		dev_err(gpr->dev, "GPR: Wrong hdr size:%d\n", hdr_size);
